          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "What It Is",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "A self-hosted binary (mongosqld) that acts as a MySQL-protocol SQL translation layer in front of MongoDB. BI tools connect via ODBC/JDBC as if connecting to a MySQL database.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-bi-connector/#what-it-is",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "DRDL Schema Files",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "mongosqld uses DRDL (Document Relational Definition Language) files to define the SQL schema mapping:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-bi-connector/#drdl-schema-files",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "EOL Timeline",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "September 2026: BI Connector reaches end-of-life; mongosqld will no longer be supported or updated",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-bi-connector/#eol-timeline",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Migration: All customers should migrate to Atlas SQL Interface (if on Atlas) or third-party tools (Hasura, DBeaver, etc.)",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-bi-connector/#eol-timeline",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Architecture",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Atlas SQL Interface uses Atlas Data Federation (FDI) as its query engine. No self-hosted binary needed.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-bi-connector/#architecture-1",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
